WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.060
Protons.

2
00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.210
Neutrons.

3
00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.400
Electrons.

4
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.670
Neutrinos.

5
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:05.820
Pions.

6
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:07.570
And the list goes on.

7
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.710
Physicists sort every one
of them into families,

8
00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.420
the way biologists sort living things.

9
00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.470
The proton and the neutron
land in one family.

10
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.860
The electron and the neutrino
land in a different one.

11
00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.580
But what decides which
family a particle belongs to?

12
00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:27.210
In this mission, you'll build
the particle family tree:

13
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.010
hadrons, baryons, mesons and leptons.

14
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:35.970
Then you'll meet the antibaryons, and
find out why a quark is never found on its

15
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:36.940
own.

16
00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:41.800
Your mission: find out what decides
which family a particle belongs to.
